hing compatibility, health and fitness features, battery life, comfort, performance and value. Its top overall pick is the Apple Watch Series 12, praised for seamless iPhone integration, smooth performance and its subscription-free Readiness Score, though its roughly 24-hour battery life may require daily charging. The Garmin Venu X1 is the best Garmin choice for runners and cyclists, offering interactive maps, detailed training tools and up to about nine days of battery life. The affordable Amazfit Active 2 delivers strong GPS and workout tracking, a bright AMOLED screen and several days of use. For premium durability and longer endurance, the Apple Watch Ultra 4 lasts around two and a half days in testing; the Apple Watch SE 3 offers core Apple Watch features at a lower price. Huawei\u2019s Watch GT 5 is another long-lasting fitness option, though availability is limited in the US. Apple Watches provide the strongest ecosystem integration, while third-party watches can offer better battery life and training depth, with some compromises in apps, messaging and data syncing. Buyers should verify feature availability by country and iOS compatibility.","ref_id":{"turn_index":374691,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":0},"pub_date":1793205079.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/JIniQMD4AR9evATntJ7B9APsrM8r7b0jg0P94FvS-k_6P-qUHYPjEeOzjccDBnrK5BTvB5ByORA5UojjEf6g-84IS4WaYaPnNvSta1ZxEOhIM4JloBYLqYUNXO98ZK5w","attribution":"www.techradar.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.womanandhome.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.womanandhome.com/health-wellbeing/best-fitbits/","title":"The best Fitbits - I've tried every one made, but these are the only 6 worth buying in 2026","snippet":"A 2026 buying guide based on five years of testing ranks six Fitbit-family devices for different needs. The Fitbit Edge is the best overall, balancing a bright screen, built-in GPS, more than 100 workout profiles, smartwatch tools and seven-day battery life for under \u00a3160. The screenless Fitbit Air is the best alternative, offering discreet wear and AI-powered health and lifestyle insights through Google Health. The Charge 6 is the strongest traditional fitness tracker, with GPS, 40 workout modes, machine connectivity and Google services. The Pixel Watch 5 is the most capable smartwatch, with advanced tracking, Gemini and useful smart features, but typically lasts only about 30 hours. The Inspire 3 is the budget choice for basic activity and health tracking, with up to 10 days\u2019 battery but no built-in GPS. The Sense 2 suits holistic health monitoring, including ECG, sleep, stress and blood-oxygen features. All listed models are water-resistant to 50 metres, but are unsuitable for diving, hot tubs and saunas. Google has shifted its smartwatch focus from Fitbit Versa and Sense lines to Pixel watches.","ref_id":{"turn_index":374691,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":14},"pub_date":1793103741.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/r6KxzvQNfKeY4z4iLbh4C7DjZVqtDvJmwzH_G-kNubONBatu5IZEASnPIXxJsJu18_-kuKDgLu8M6CKWBTm7jIhpDO4oRq3LRl4sOPP8dBlmMUW15qo3bhRwqys19W-a","attribution":"www.womanandhome.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.popularmechanics.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.popularmechanics.com/technology/gear/a74248921/how-apple-watch-12-tracks-heart-rate-24-7/","title":"How Apple Built Watch Series 12 to Track Heart Rate 24/7-Without Nuking Battery Life","snippet":"Apple\u2019s Watch Series 12 and Ultra 4 use redesigned optical sensors to measure heart rate about every five seconds and HRV 24 times more often, without reducing battery life. Four larger green LEDs improve readings during daytime and exercise, while red and infrared LEDs serve lower-motion periods and blood-oxygen sensing. Eight surrounding photodiodes and a newly molded zirconia back crystal help capture reflected light while blocking stray light. Apple says efficiency gains in hardware, computation, and machine-learning algorithms\u2014adapted from AirPods work\u2014make frequent monitoring possible without a larger battery. The author\u2019s running tests found the Ultra 4\u2019s readings closely tracked chest-strap data, though chest straps remain more accurate, especially during rapid interval changes. The Watch sometimes leaves gaps in its records when its confidence-checking algorithm cannot verify a reading; Apple says it prefers missing data to unreliable estimates. More continuous heart-rate and HRV data may help users notice patterns related to hydration, caffeine, illness, sleep, and recovery. Overall, the upgrades make wrist-based monitoring more useful while preserving battery life.","ref_id":{"turn_index":374691,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":15},"pub_date":1793133210.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/0aUFlupZmdXOLyAzm84Ksv1n2Vb10Aw3dOTFPiQFqemYuDwM6QVVWU2rU2581ddGZPqF4Hv61qYIvSCGWbRfS-c6IzQe_OIjMbbzHd-QCKAAR6c25Ht8z9z5LoXPPrblebKgnhqzopK2x-6t6883uafETH8KpxqosGSbrUz_5tATUTw5vLQ2nVFiQ7Nd3WtR","attribution":"www.popularmechanics.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.tomsguide.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.tomsguide.com/sales-events/apples-new-devices-are-up-for-preorder-but-these-21-deals-are-available-now","title":"Apple's new devices are up for preorder, but these 21 deals are available now","snippet":"Apple has announced new devices, including the iPad mini 8, iMac M6 and MacBook Pro M6, which are available for preorder. While shoppers wait, the article highlights 21 discounts on existing Apple products, spanning accessories, AirPods, Apple Watches, Macs, iPads and MacBooks. Notable offers include $50 off the iPad mini 7, $150 off the 14-inch MacBook Pro, and $50 off the 11-inch base iPad, now $399. Other deals include the Apple Watch 11 at $379 (down from $429), the Mac Studio M5 Max at $2,299 (a $200 reduction), and both 13- and 15-inch MacBook Air M5 models discounted by $150. Accessories include reduced-price AirTags, a USB-C power adapter, charging cable and Apple Pencil. The article also features AirPods Pro 3 and AirPods Max 2, plus newer Apple Watch, Mac mini and iPad Air models. It emphasizes that discounts apply to both current and previous-generation devices, offering savings across a broad range of budgets and needs.","ref_id":{"turn_index":374691,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":16},"pub_date":1793202114.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/XRVc6uSKBoXlZMc-mnOx7FPwoXQBE_AvVLWbUi6wfZO-ENc_wAxyCii9X2Y4BAZtBaq15xtmqhAT0akDBjre6zpane9HI3CT_K9FFqdGHdQQGYNZGLjDZZWUyITKzuU8","attribution":"www.tomsguide.com"},{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.tomsguide.com/wellness/fitness-trackers/i-just-went-hands-on-with-the-garmin-cirqa-and-it-strikes-a-near-perfect-balance-between-the-fitbit-air-and-whoop-5-0","title":"Garmin Cirqa review: I wore the screen-free Garmin Cirqa for two weeks, and it's a near-perfect balance between the entry-level Fitbit Air and pro-level Whoop 5.0","snippet":"After more than two weeks of testing, the reviewer finds Garmin\u2019s $199 screen-free Cirqa a strong middle ground between the $99 Fitbit Air and subscription-based Whoop 5.0. It offers core health and fitness features without a subscription, with optional Garmin Connect+ insights costing $6.99 monthly or $69.99 annually. The Cirqa is larger than the Fitbit, but comfortable, lightweight, water-resistant to 50 meters, and lasts about 10 days per charge. Its health tracking earns high marks: sleep and heart-rate readings closely matched the Fitbit Air, while Garmin provides richer sleep, women\u2019s health, recovery, readiness, and Body Battery metrics. Fitness tracking is generally accurate, including elevation, and the physical button enables quick workout starts; however, it lacks GPS and relies on a paired phone for outdoor location data. Drawbacks include a scratchy, slow-drying strap, difficult strap changes, and costly replacement bands. Overall, the Cirqa costs more than the Fitbit Air but delivers substantially more detailed, actionable insights without requiring a subscription, making it a worthwhile upgrade for users seeking advanced tracking without Whoop\u2019s ongoing fees.","ref_id":{"turn_index":374691,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":19},"pub_date":1786075875.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/9UyO2ODHRF3b9gN-R_c_T62L2KrMbbLgSHbcgoBQy4hba9HeE4Ym0BNuyypYe-uT6Xqq5wz6xQ-D-6AqXCbHIVS7VgZSmj0uImlRppGTlCtC3shm7LAOViDqptKreOTM","attribution":"www.tomsguide.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.aboutdarwin.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.aboutdarwin.com/best-smartwatches-under-200-dollars/","title":"8 Best Smartwatches Under $200 (November 2026) Tested","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":374691,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":1},"pub_date":1791331200.0,"attribution":"www.aboutdarwin.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.beastcompare.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.beastcompare.com/amazon-finds/best-cheap-smartwatches","title":"Best Smartwatches Under $200 (2026): Cheap Picks","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":374691,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":2},"pub_date":1792022400.0,"attribution":"www.beastcompare.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"smartgearpick.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://smartgearpick.com/guides/best-smartwatches-under-200","title":"Best Smartwatches Under $200 (2026) \u2014 Top Value Picks | SmartGearPick","snippet":"","ref_id":{"turn_index":374691,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":3},"pub_date":null,"attribution":"smartgearpick.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.livescience.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.livescience.com/best-fitness-tracker","title":"Best fitness trackers 2026: From smart rings to multisport GPS watches","snippet":"Live Science\u2019s 2026 fitness-tracker guide compares tested wearables for different needs, budgets, and activity levels. The Amazfit Balance is the overall winner, offering accurate health tracking, a lightweight design, extensive wellness features, and 14-day battery life for about $199. The Garmin Fenix 8 is the premium choice for serious athletes and outdoor adventurers, with advanced metrics, maps, GPS, durability, and 16-day battery life, though it costs around $1,000. Budget buyers should consider the Xiaomi Smart Band 10, which provides 150-plus workout modes, reliable basic tracking, and up to 21 days of battery life. Other recommendations include the Garmin Forerunner 965 for runners, Suunto Vertical 2 as a cheaper Garmin alternative, Xiaomi Watch 5 as a Pixel Watch alternative, Oura Ring Gen 4 for highly accurate sleep and recovery tracking, Whoop MG for screen-free detailed monitoring, and Garmin Vivoactive 6 for beginners. The guide emphasizes that trackers can support motivation and healthier habits, but calorie, blood-oxygen, sleep-apnea, blood-pressure, and heart-condition readings have limitations and should not replace medical evaluation. Buyers should prioritize intended use, GPS, durability, battery life, smart features, and budget.","ref_id":{"turn_index":374691,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":17},"pub_date":1776161416.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/uS_2efxPQw8l3MPY_wpwWkOJZJoqXkATCe4nP9HLuXagvPdddMQL1fnz8zcdxC3htA-ugxhaxw4C5D-ubT4p26olcxQpt-XRH4_esXJMwykOiWECKx20LabmBNEuzqTS","attribution":"www.livescience.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"nymag.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://nymag.com/strategist/article/best-smartwatches.html?utm_campaign=feed-part&utm_medium=social_acct&utm_source=rss","title":"The 8 Very Best Smartwatches","snippet":"Actualizada el 16 de enero de 2026, esta gu\u00eda recomienda ocho de los mejores relojes inteligentes seg\u00fan el sistema operativo, las necesidades deportivas y el presupuesto. Los smartwatches combinan seguimiento de la salud y la actividad f\u00edsica con funciones del tel\u00e9fono, como notificaciones, llamadas, aplicaciones, m\u00fasica y pagos sin contacto. La elecci\u00f3n ideal depende de la compatibilidad con el m\u00f3vil, las funciones de salud y la autonom\u00eda.\n\nLas principales recomendaciones son:\n- **Apple Watch SE 3 (240 d\u00f3lares):** mejor opci\u00f3n general para iPhone, con pantalla siempre activa, seguimiento de salud y buen rendimiento a un precio asequible.\n- **Apple Watch Series 11 (390 d\u00f3lares):** alternativa pr\u00e9mium para iOS, con ECG, medici\u00f3n de ox\u00edgeno en sangre y mayor autonom\u00eda.\n- **Apple Watch Ultra 3 (780 d\u00f3lares):** opci\u00f3n resistente para aventuras al aire libre, con bater\u00eda de hasta 42 horas y comunicaciones por sat\u00e9lite.\n- **Samsung Galaxy Watch8 Classic (500 d\u00f3lares):** mejor para usuarios de Samsung, con bisel giratorio y funciones avanzadas.\n- **Google Pixel Watch 4 (350-400 d\u00f3lares):** ideal para otros tel\u00e9fonos Android, con bater\u00eda reemplazable y hasta 40 horas de autonom\u00eda.\n- **Samsung Galaxy Watch Ultra (650 d\u00f3lares):** alternativa resistente para Android.\n- **Garmin V\u00edvoactive 6 (300 d\u00f3lares):** mejor para fitness, con hasta 11 d\u00edas de bater\u00eda.\n- **Garmin Fenix 8 AMOLED Sapphire (1.090 d\u00f3lares):** opci\u00f3n deportiva avanzada, con GPS preciso, mapas y hasta 16 d\u00edas de autonom\u00eda.","ref_id":{"turn_index":374691,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":18},"pub_date":1768928400.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/x_jVcwP-efA7CshsH6kMgn0Y9Qh2cmzkAmiHCjBL3ZYFa4R9N6LNNwDo54LpwLvmFT6Q2YY575trKpatA4YBFDKfYrTe2-iGDUwpJbe7EKymb4jiSUDdK6YonsEPj_UBguqN3i8gfqddhw5PCzroX99PW55RqTKRGPizNTnkymSujsdMX5RIDKZ3xVdY8vGn","attribution":"nymag.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"nypost.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://nypost.com/health/best-fitness-trackers-review/","title":"Are wearables legit? We stress-tested the best fitness trackers and had an expert weigh in","snippet":"The article argues that fitness wearables are useful when their data leads to better health decisions\u2014not simply more tracking. Expert Gary Brecka says key measures include heart-rate variability, resting heart rate, sleep quality and consistency, and respiratory rate; users should focus on trends rather than a single readiness score. Wearables may flag meaningful changes but are not doctors or substitutes for medical care.\n\nThe guide highlights five devices for different needs: Oura Ring 5 for discreet sleep and health tracking, with up to seven days\u2019 battery life and a $6 monthly subscription; WHOOP 5.0 for screen-free recovery and strain insights, with up to 14 days\u2019 battery life and memberships from $199 annually; Garmin Forerunner 970 for serious athletes seeking heart-rate accuracy and advanced GPS; Apple Watch Ultra 2 for an intuitive, versatile smartwatch with safety features but relatively frequent charging; and Samsung Galaxy Watch Ultra for rugged outdoor use, though its battery lasts about three days.\n\nBrecka favors passive tracking that provides clear, actionable guidance. Subscriptions may be worthwhile when they interpret data and recommend useful actions, rather than merely collecting metrics.","ref_id":{"turn_index":374691,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":20},"pub_date":1783607400.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://nypost.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/07/watches.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&resize=500","attribution":"nypost.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.goodhousekeeping.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.goodhousekeeping.com/life/money/g69410530/apple-watch-black-friday-deals-2025/","title":"4 Apple Watches Are Already On Sale Ahead of Black Friday","snippet":"Ahead of Black Friday 2025, four Apple Watches are discounted on Amazon. The Apple Watch Series 10 starts at $279.99, with savings of up to 30% depending on band and cellular options. Good Housekeeping reviewers praise its slim, lightweight design, bright Always-On display, battery life and swim tracking. The second-generation Apple Watch SE is $159.99, offering core features such as heart-rate and sleep tracking, water resistance and crash detection, but no Always-On display, ECG or blood-oxygen readings. The pink Series 9 is $191.61, a 26% discount; it supports many workout types and health metrics and was previously rated the publication\u2019s top fitness tracker for iPhone users. The newest SE 3 is $199.99 in white, 20% off. It adds an Always-On display, faster performance and gesture controls; cellular models are not discounted. Good Housekeeping says its Tech Lab regularly tests smartwatches and fitness trackers, while its commerce editor reviews Black Friday offers to identify worthwhile deals.","ref_id":{"turn_index":374691,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":21},"pub_date":1762985280.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/grgrJT7gPrhl1bstFSJ1VBsBb9L_LHGLsGrSmRjIJib_lAV7e8caRWWv7RGluSWrp1gvDh-eH1Vli0D1-P_8JlfZU4pOL9VOWtBNcrCft4iZKCfPf5g3vj3BnNGipXQjPXwO1Pf-5i5KyV2VBHGz6bwjSnOUd2K5_V0i9q2XmD0u5FxrZawadDRvOKD14br_","attribution":"www.goodhousekeeping.com"}]}]},"reasoning_start_time":1793646558.996752,"streaming_parent_id":"efb10bff-8319-415b-b6b6-4c20764648d6","streaming_parent_revision":0,"model_switcher_deny":[]},"recipient":"all","channel":null},"conversation_id":"6ae8dfde-4fb4-83e8-ac92-9b2a3900e0af","error":null,"error_code":null},"c":14}

